{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536405-bg3-to-vtm","id":1536405,"title":"BG3 to VtM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-27T22:50:34-07:00","id":1536405,"title":"BG3 to VtM","content":"Was pondering both Baldur's Gate 3 and VtM earlier and the idea that Astarion would be a Toreador with the Scene Queen predator type came to mind. That got me thinking, what about the other companions? Here's how it broken down:<br /> <br /> Karlach - Brujah, naturally.<br /> <br /> Gale - Tremere<br /> <br /> Shadowheart - Lasombra or a Ministry told she was Lasombra.<br /> <br /> Wyll - Banu Haqim<br /> <br /> Lae'zel - Also Banu Haqim<br /> <br /> Halsin - Gangrel, just as nature intended.<br /> <br /> Jaheira - Also a gangrel, but more tempered.<br /> <br /> Minsc - Malkavian<br /> <br /> Minthara - Trickier, but I want to say Ministry. A spurned one though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yay, nay, additions, or alternatives?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 05-28-2024, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T08:40:16-07:00","id":1536430,"title":"","content":"It did reminds me of a very weird, but fun, game I played once.<br /> <br /> The premise was that a group of Mages managed to create a huge spaceship capable of exploring really distant worlds with the intention of getting as many people as possible to escape the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> So the PCs, of many splats, were refugees in a D&amp;D world. It was originally to <i>Tormenta</i>, a Brazilian setting, but it could easily be adapted to Forgotten Realms, taking place at the Sword Coast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T10:12:44-07:00","id":1536442,"title":"","content":"I can dig it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T15:34:08-07:00","id":1536470,"title":"","content":"I'm going to assume spoilers are okay for this thread.<br /> <br /> Will is probably the trickiest. There isn't a very obvious or easy correlation between the Warlock class and any of the Vampire Clans. I'd probably make him a Ventrue (leaning into their knightly aspect vs his Father's more traditional lordly aspect) with Dark Thaumaturgy and a demonic patron. He hasn't sold his soul just yet but it's getting close...<br /> <br /> Balthazar works almost too well as a Giovanni. He's even got that whole creepy thing going with his brother and his mother. He keeps his family close. <br /> <br /> Ketheric is obviously a Cappadocian.<br /> <br /> Orin fits well as a nutty Malkavian Antitribu, though she needs Viscissitude for Horrid Form to represent her Slayer transformation.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm not too sure about Gortash. He's a greasy manipulator and string puller, but his class is Barbarian. I guess he could work as a Ventrue or a Brujah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T15:56:30-07:00","id":1536471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536405-bg3-to-vtm?p=1536470#post1536470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to assume spoilers are okay for this thread.<br /> <br /> Will is probably the trickiest. There isn't a very obvious or easy correlation between the Warlock class and any of the Vampire Clans. I'd probably make him a Ventrue (leaning into their knightly aspect vs his Father's more traditional lordly aspect) with Dark Thaumaturgy and a demonic patron. He hasn't sold his soul just yet but it's getting close...</div> </div> </div> </div>Tzimisce koldun. The deal with Kupala is solid warlock material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist"